ose Story-level requirements number 4, 3, 3, 3, 3, 7, 3, 5, 4 and 5 respectively, and every Epic-level requirement is carried by at least one Story.","evidence":"The grep for Epic-level requirements returned 13 matches, FR001 to FR013, at DEF.md:27-39. The grep for Story-level requirements returned 40 matches across S001 to S010, and the per-Story counts match the premise exactly: S001 has 4 (DEF.md:43-46), S002 has 3 (50-52), S003 has 3 (56-58), S004 has 3 (62-64), S005 has 3 (68-70), S006 has 7 (74-80), S007 has 3 (84-86), S008 has 5 (90-94), S009 has 4 (98-101) and S010 has 5 (105-109). Coverage also holds on the matched text: FR001 is carried by S001:FR001 (line 43), FR002 by S001:FR002 (44), FR003 by S001:FR004 (46), FR004 by S002:FR001-FR003 (50-52), FR005 by S003:FR001-FR003 (56-58), FR006 by S004:FR001-FR002 (62-63), FR007 by S005:FR001-FR002 (68-69), FR008 by S006:FR001-FR003 (74-76), FR009 by S006:FR005 (78), FR010 by S007:FR001 (84), FR011 by S008:FR001-FR003 (90-92), FR012 by S009:FR001-FR002 (98-99) and FR013 by S010:FR001, FR002 and FR004 (105, 106, 108). The four anchors (FR001, FR013, S001, S010) all resolve in DEF.md.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p32","ref":"k7, 6. Stories","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"The Story dependencies are s2→s1; s7→s1,s2; s8→s1,s7; s9→s2; s10→s7; they are acyclic and every enrichment Story (s7-s10) depends, directly or transitively, on a completeness/consistency Story, as constraint k7 requires, while s3-s6 declare no dependency.","evidence":"UNVERIFIABLE from the gathered evidence. The only probe was an unscoped grep for /Depends on:/ which returned 50 matches and was TRUNCATED at the cap. Every returned match belongs to a different epic's DEF.md/HLD.md (add-bugfix-triage-category-…E202609181703991c, add-build-workflow-…E20260717185807ba, add-daemon-driven-code-review-stage-…E20260803761a43a6, add-module-test-health-analyzer-…E202607298f485fe5, add-plan-workflow-…E202607151cd9a4c3, build-deployment-design-framework-…E20260721753e0ed6). None of them shows the claimed edge set (s2→s1; s7→s1,s2; s8→s1,s7; s9→s2; s10→s7): no returned line reads `s1`, `s2` for an s7, `s1`, `s7` for an s8, or `s7` for an s10, and no returned epic is shown to have ten Stories. The closest lines (e.g. add-daemon-driven-code-review-stage DEF.md:158 `s2`, `s3`, `s4`, `s5`; DEF.md:180 and :195 `s6`) do not match the premise. No read of the artifact's own '6. Stories' section or of constraint k7 was supplied, so the dependency list, its acyclicity, the k7 requirement that s7-s10 depend on a completeness/consistency Story, and the absence of dependencies on s3-s6 cannot be confirmed or contradicted. The edge set as stated in the premise is internally acyclic (s1 ← s2 ← s9; s1,s2 ← s7 ← s8,s10) and each of s7-s10 does reach s1 or s2, but whether that matches the artifact text and whether s1/s2 are the completeness/consistency Stories is not shown by the evidence.","action":"Re-run the probe scoped to the artifact under review rather than the whole docs/epics tree: grep /Depends on:/ restricted to this Epic's DEF.md, plus path:line reads of its '6. Stories' section (the s1-s10 headings and their Depends-on lines) and of the k7 constraint text. Then confirm (a) the five dependency lines match s2→s1; s7→s1,s2; s8→s1,s7; s9→s2; s10→s7, (b) s3-s6 carry no Depends-on line, and (c) s1 and/or s2 are the completeness/consistency Stories k7 refers to. No artifact edit is warranted until that evidence exists.","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence does not include the artifact's own Story section or k7 text; the grep was unscoped and truncated at the 50-match cap on other epics' files, so no evidence-derived text correction can be made. The premise needs a re-probe, not an edit.","options":["Re-run the Depends-on grep scoped to this Epic's DEF.md path so the cap is not consumed by other epics, and re-judge the premise against those lines.","Add path:line reads of the artifact's '6. Stories' section (s1-s10) and the k7 constraint, then verify the edge set, the acyclicity, and that s3-s6 declare no dependency.","Accept with a note that the ordering premise is unverified by the deterministic probe and was checked by hand against the artifact's Story section."]}},{"claimId":"p33","ref":"4. Assumptions / s8/lc1","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"Subsystem grouping (s8) is computed from the stored relationships, so it must follow the fix for lost relationships (s1); enrichment built before s1 would rest on a graph that ISSUE-12f70133 shows is missing most cross-file edges.","evidence":"The factual basis of the ordering is confirmed by the gathered evidence. ISSUE.md:23 states that a resolved edge is silently dropped when its target is not stored yet: `upsertResolvedRelations` (`src/db/relations.ts:120-154`) counts the edge as skipped and continues, logging at debug level only. The grep confirms that function exists at src/db/relations.ts:120, with the skip log at src/db/relations.ts:151 ('skipped edges with missing endpoints or unknown kind'). The cited anchor ISSUE.md:27 resolves to the intended text: 'A reindex cannot repair it', because `indexFile` returns early for files with an unchanged content hash and `fullIndex` calls it without cleanFirst, so lost import edges are never rebuilt. The issue directory slug ('bug-code-graph-missing-most-cross-…') matches the 'missing most cross-file edges' wording. Together these show the stored graph lacks cross-file edges until the s1 fix lands, so anything derived from stored relationships (s8) must come after s1. The evidence does not show s8's own implementation, but that s8 reads stored relationships is the artifact's design statement rather than a claim about existing source.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p34","ref":"5. Constraints / 6. Stories","kind":"closed-union","severity":"MED","premise":"Every constraint id an